      ],
      "data": {
        "text": "A white star is fed back into itself, and each pass shrinks, turns and shifts its colour a little. That makes a glowing tunnel.\nThe Deflection Yoke then bends the picture like a wobbling monitor.\nSlow LFOs breathe the star's size and points, and sway the tunnel's turn and zoom.\nTry the Feedback knobs: GAIN, ZOOM, ROTATE and HUE per pass. Press the clear button after big changes.\nTry the Deflection Yoke DEPTH and RATE knobs."
      }
    }
